#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_world.HexWorld:1 of
msgid "A world that consists of hexagonal tiles."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_world.HexWorld:3 of
msgid ""
"Hexes are addressed with offset coordinates `(column, row)`, like tiles "
"in a TiledWorld. Odd rows are shifted half a hex to the right (pointy-top"
" layout). Actors can also be placed on corners (shared by up to three "
"hexes) or edges (shared by two hexes)."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_world.HexWorld:8 of
msgid ""
"The six neighbors of a hex are reached with the directions `\"o\"`, "
"`\"so\"`, `\"sw\"`, `\"w\"`, `\"nw\"`, `\"no\"`. Because odd rows are "
"shifted, the diagonal neighbors depend on the row parity:"
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_world.HexWorld:12 of
msgid ""
"Odd rows: `\"no\"` and `\"so\"` point to `(column + 1, row - 1)` and "
"`(column + 1, row + 1)`, while `\"nw\"` and `\"sw\"` point to `(column, "
"row - 1)` and `(column, row + 1)`."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_world.HexWorld:15 of
msgid ""
"Even rows: `\"no\"` and `\"so\"` point to `(column, row - 1)` and "
"`(column, row + 1)`, while `\"nw\"` and `\"sw\"` point to `(column - 1, "
"row - 1)` and `(column - 1, row + 1)`."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_world.HexWorld:19 of
msgid ""
"`\"o\"` and `\"w\"` always point to `(column + 1, row)` and `(column - 1,"
" row)`."
msgstr ""

