"Click and pixel detection for actors on hexes uses the exact hex picking "
"inherited from the tiled sensor manager. Actors on corners or edges are "
"detected when the pixel is close to the corner or edge center, so "
"settlements and roads can be clicked."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_world_sensor_manager.HexWorldSensorManager:8
#: of
msgid ""
"Distances between actors on hexes are hex distances (number of hexes "
"between the positions), not euclidean offset distances."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_world_sensor_manager.HexWorldSensorManager:11
#: of
msgid ""
"Movement along the six hex axes (the directions `\"no\"`, `\"o\"`, "
"`\"so\"`, `\"sw\"`, `\"w\"`, `\"nw\"` and their scratch-style degrees) "
"moves from hex to hex in cube coordinates, so every step is exactly one "
"hex, independent of the row parity. Angles that are not hex axes are "
"snapped to the nearest axis (`hex_coords.nearest_axis_degrees`), so a "
"single step never jumps more than one hex."
msgstr ""

