#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_coords:1 of
msgid "Coordinate mathematics for hexagonal worlds."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_coords:3 of
msgid ""
"HexWorld uses a pointy-top layout with odd-r offset coordinates: Students"
" address hexes with `(column, row)` tuples, exactly like tiles in a "
"TiledWorld. Odd rows are shifted half a hex to the right."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_coords:7 of
msgid ""
"Internally, cube coordinates `(q, r, s)` with `q + r + s = 0` are used "
"for neighbor and distance calculations, because they are uniform across "
"rows."
msgstr ""

